course: dictionary
lesson: 14438
title: A word from a town
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words come from places. Paisley is a town in Scotland, near Glasgow, and it gave its name to a pattern. The pattern is made of curved, teardrop shapes, often with smaller patterns inside them. Paisley can be a noun for the pattern, and an adjective, as in «a paisley tie».
explain: The pattern is older than the name it has today. It came from Persia and India, and weavers in Paisley copied it in the 1800s, so people began to call it after their town. You can spot it on shirts, ties, scarves and bandanas. With a small p, paisley is the pattern. With a capital P, Paisley is the town.
explain: Context helps you here too. «Her scarf had red and gold paisley swirls.» The word paisley tells you the kind of pattern, and the word swirls tells you the shape. Read the words around a new word to check that your meaning fits.
fact: Paisley is a pattern of curved, teardrop shapes.
fact: With a small p, paisley is the pattern; with a capital P, Paisley is the town in Scotland, near Glasgow.
fact: The pattern came from Persia and India, and weavers in Paisley copied it in the 1800s.
fact: In «a paisley tie», paisley is an adjective: it describes the tie.
fact: If a sentence mentions shirts, ties or scarves, paisley is probably a pattern.
exercise: «Dad wore a blue shirt with a paisley pattern.» What is paisley here? | *A pattern of curved, teardrop shapes | A large stone wall | A bird that sings at night | A loud noise
exercise: Ava says, «Paisley is a town in Scotland, so the pattern is named after a town.» Which town gave the pattern its name? | London | Persia | *Paisley | Edinburgh
exercise: In «Ella bought a paisley scarf», what kind of word is paisley? | A number | *An adjective, describing the scarf | A name of a person | A verb, showing an action
test: Where is the town of Paisley? | In Persia, far to the east | In Wales, by the sea | *In Scotland, near Glasgow | In London, by the river
test: Why is the pattern called paisley? | It is named after a Scottish king | *Weavers in the town of Paisley copied it in the 1800s | It was invented in London in 1900 | It is named after a bird
exam: What does paisley mean in «Her scarf was red with white paisley patterns»? | A cold, wet day | A town in London | *A pattern of curved, teardrop shapes | A kind of red flower
